## Speed sweep

served `intarsia-35b`, fingerprint `None`, ctx 20480, 3 reps, 128 forced output tokens

| prompt tok | TTFT s | prefill tok/s | marginal prefill | decode tok/s | peak decode | server prefill | server decode | out tok |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 992 | 0.19 | 5327 (5210–5391) * | - | 83.6 (83.5–83.7) | 85.8 (85.6–87.0) | - | - | 128 |
| 4090 | 0.61 | 6678 (6662–6708) | 7272 | 81.1 (80.7–81.2) | 82.9 (82.7–87.7) | - | - | 128 |
| 16656 | 2.73 | 6105 (6095–6121) | 5936 | 73.6 (73.6–73.7) | 74.8 (74.5–75.5) | - | - | 128 |

\* under 1024 uncached prompt tokens: TTFT is per-request overhead, not prefill throughput.

Marginal prefill = Δprompt tokens / ΔTTFT from the previous row; fixed request overhead cancels, so it is the cleanest prefill throughput figure.

Peak decode = fastest 32-token stretch of each call (burst speed, e.g. a run of accepted speculative drafts); median and range over reps. '-' = older run or output too short.


## Method

Streamed OpenAI-compatible calls, temperature 0. TTFT = request start to first content/reasoning token; prefill tok/s = uncached prompt_tokens / TTFT; decode tok/s = (completion_tokens - 1) / (last - first token), counts from server usage. Speed sweep: fresh nonce first in every prompt (no prefix-cache hits), ignore_eos+min_tokens forces the full length, 1 discarded warmup, median of reps. Other clients' in-flight requests checked before every sweep call. Quality-run speed is incidental (varying prompts), not a sweep.

